# Web Frontend Patterns (apps/web)

## Project Layout

No `src/` directory — all paths resolve from `app/` root via `@/` alias.

```
app/
  (auth)/           → public routes (login, verify-otp)
  (private)/        → authenticated + sidebar (dashboard, admin/, teacher/, student/)
  (exam)/           → authenticated, no sidebar (exam-portal/[id]/)
components/         → shared UI shells (not primitives — those are @examhell/ui)
hooks/
  api/              → one file per resource
  custom/           → use-chat, use-debounce, use-query-params, …
lib/                → api.ts, firebase.ts, tanstack.ts, dayjs.ts
providers/          → AuthProvider, QueryProvider, ArtifactPanelProvider, AppProviders
types/              → api.ts, tanstack.ts, models/
constants/          → env.ts, common.ts
config/             → navigation.ts, data-table.ts
```

## API Hooks (hooks/api/)

One file per resource. Pattern: plain async function → `api.*` (Axios) → wrapped in `useQuery` / `useMutation`.

**Types** (from `types/api.ts` and `types/tanstack.ts`):

```ts
type TApiPromise<TData = undefined> = Promise<TApiSuccess<TData>> | Promise<TApiError>
type TApiSuccess<TData = undefined> = { message: string; data?: TData; pagination?: TPaginationResponse }
type TApiError = { message: string; status_code: number }

type TQueryOpts<TResponse, TSelect = TApiSuccess<TResponse>> =
  Omit<UseQueryOptions<TApiSuccess<TResponse>, TApiError, TSelect>, "queryKey" | "queryFn">

type TMutationOpts<TVariables = void, TResponse = undefined> =
  Omit<UseMutationOptions<TApiSuccess<TResponse>, TApiError, TVariables>, "mutationKey" | "mutationFn">
```

**Full CRUD hook file pattern:**

```ts
// hooks/api/exam.ts

// Query function (plain async)
const getAllExams = (params: TGetAllExamsParams): TApiPromise<TExam[]> =>
  api.get("/exams", { params })

// useQuery hook
export const useGetAllExams = (
  params: TGetAllExamsParams,
  options?: TQueryOpts<TExam[]>
) =>
  useQuery({
    queryKey: ["useGetAllExams", params],    // key = hook name + params
    queryFn: () => getAllExams(params),
    ...options,
  })

// Mutation function
const createExam = (exam: TCreateExamPayload): TApiPromise<TExam> =>
  api.post("/exams", exam)

// useMutation hook
export const useCreateExam = (options?: TMutationOpts<TCreateExamPayload, TExam>) =>
  useMutation({
    mutationKey: ["useCreateExam"],
    mutationFn: createExam,
    ...options,
  })
```

**Rules:**
- Query keys are always `[hookName, ...params]` — name the key after the hook exactly
- Accept optional `TQueryOpts` / `TMutationOpts` — callers pass `onSuccess`, `onError`, `enabled` etc.
- Never call `invalidateQueries` inside a hook — callers handle cache invalidation in `onSuccess`
- All hooks are named exports — no default exports

## Axios API Client (lib/api.ts)

```ts
const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", "ngrok-skip-browser-warning": "true" },
})

// Request interceptor — attach Firebase ID token automatically
api.interceptors.request.use(async (config) => {
  const idToken = auth.currentUser ? await getIdToken(auth.currentUser) : null
  if (idToken && !config.headers.Authorization) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${idToken}`
  return config
})

// Response interceptor — unwrap to { message, data, pagination }
api.interceptors.response.use(
  (res) => res.data,
  (err: AxiosError) => Promise.reject(err?.response?.data)
)
```

AI chat uses **raw `fetch`** with SSE — never Axios for streaming endpoints:

```ts
const res = await fetch(`${env.NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_URL}/chats/${conversationId}/completion`, {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", Authorization: `Bearer ${idToken}` },
  body: JSON.stringify({ prompt, user_files: files }),
})
// read as ReadableStream and parse SSE manually in use-chat.ts
```

## TanStack Query Config (lib/tanstack.ts)

```ts
export const queryClient = new QueryClient({
  defaultOptions: {
    queries: { retry: 0, staleTime: 3000, refetchOnWindowFocus: false },
  },
})
export const invalidateQueries = (filters?: InvalidateQueryFilters) =>
  queryClient.invalidateQueries(filters)
```

Use `invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["useGetAllExams"] })` in mutation `onSuccess` to refresh lists.

## Firebase Auth (lib/firebase.ts + providers/auth-provider.tsx)

```ts
// lib/firebase.ts
const app = getApps().length ? getApps()[0] : initializeApp(firebaseConfig)
export const auth = getAuth(app)
```

**AuthProvider** syncs Firebase user → DB on every auth state change:

```ts
// On login: POST /auth/sync with Bearer token → get TSession + is_new flag
const syncUserToDB = async (firebase_user: User) => {
  const token = await firebase_user.getIdToken()
  const res = await fetch(`${env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/auth/sync`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ role: localStorage.getItem("active_role") ?? "student" }),
  })
  // setSession(), setIsNewUser(), then force-refresh token for custom claims
  const claims = await firebase_user.getIdTokenResult(true)
  setRole(claims.claims.role as UserRole)
}
```

Auth state available via `useAuth()` hook — never read `auth.currentUser` directly in components.

## Route Protection

```ts
// app/(private)/layout.tsx
const { user, isLoading } = useAuth()
useEffect(() => {
  if (!isLoading && !user) router.push("/login")
}, [user, isLoading, router])
if (isLoading || !user) return <Spinner />
```

Role-based navigation defined in `config/navigation.ts` (`teacherNavItems`, `studentNavItems`, `adminNavItems`). Never hardcode nav items in components.

## Components

- **Shared shells** live in `components/` — `MainContainer`, `DataTable`, `AppSidebar`
- **Feature components** are co-located under their route folder
- **UI primitives** come from `@examhell/ui` — never recreate Shadcn/Radix locally
- Use `MainContainer` for all private pages — it provides breadcrumb + scroll area

```tsx
// Typical page structure
export default function ExamsPage() {
  const { data, isLoading } = useGetAllExams({ page: 1, limit: 20 })
  return (
    <MainContainer breadcrumbItems={[{ label: "Exams" }]}>
      {isLoading ? <Spinner /> : <DataTable columns={columns} data={data?.data ?? []} />}
    </MainContainer>
  )
}
```

## Date Formatting

Always use `src/lib/dayjs.ts` for dates — never `new Date().toLocaleDateString()` or raw `Date` formatting.

## State Management

| type | tool |
|---|---|
| Server / async data | TanStack Query |
| Global app state | React Context (`AuthProvider`, `ArtifactPanelProvider`) |
| URL / filter state | `useQueryParams` (nuqs) |
| Local UI state | `useState` |
| Persistent user prefs | `localStorage` (active_role, redirect-url) |

**Do not use `useMemo` or `useCallback`** — the React Compiler handles memoization automatically.

## Environment Variables (constants/env.ts)

```ts
export const env = {
  NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL || "NA",
  NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL || "NA",   // crud server
  NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_URL:  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_URL  || "NA",   // ai server
}
```

Always read env via `env.*` — never `process.env.*` inline in components.
